==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|bine|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|bini|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*biniz}}, representing an ''-n-'' variant of Germanic {{term/t|gem-pro|*bijō}}.  Compare Upper German and {{etyl|gsw|-}} {{term|Beie||bee|lang=de|lang=gsw}}. Cognate with {{etyl|bar|-}} {{term|Bein||bee|lang=bar}}, {{etyl|osx|-}} {{term|bini|lang=osx}}.

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f||Bienen}}

# [[bee]]
# cute, sexy woman

